        {
          "kicker": "Squad selection",
          "heading": "Jake White names Nathan Hughes in Fiji squad with four uncapped players",
          "body": "Former England international Nathan Hughes is back in Fiji's frame, drafted into Jake White's 35-man extended squad for the Nations Championship after winning 22 England caps between 2016 and 2019. White has also named four uncapped players, and could hand Peniami Narisia, Marika Parker and Setareki Bituniyata their first Test caps this month. Ben Volavola keeps his place after ending a three-year wait for a Test cap against Japan last weekend, as Fiji look to climb off the bottom of the Southern Hemisphere pool."
