          "kicker": "Squad newcomer",
          "heading": "Jamie Benson recalls shock of Andy Farrell's July call before joining Ulster",
          "body": "Jamie Benson has described a swift rise that began with a surprise call from Andy Farrell. The 24-year-old, then at Harlequins and already in an England A squad, was summoned to Ireland training in July before he had even joined Ulster. \"Obviously, it was a bit of a shock to be called in here before I'd even set foot in Ulster, but it was a great feeling,\" he says. The versatile back has impressed for Ulster and is now in the Ireland squad for the Nations Championship campaign."
